    "cell_type": "code",
    "source": "import numpy as np\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nimport scipy.stats as stats\nimport pandas as pd\nimport seaborn as sns\nimport zipfile",
    "execution_count": 297
  },
  {
    "id": "25791f787982473abe52213b4070ef69",
    "cell_type": "markdown",
    "source": "# Data Engineering"
  },
  {
    "id": "d4218f23883a496681a2278c23c2d2a3",
    "cell_type": "code",
    "source": "# Reading the data from a text file and saving to Pandas DataFrame\nwith zipfile.ZipFile('data/task1/jetnet_logs.zip') as myzip:\n    with myzip.open('jetnet_logs.txt') as myfile:\n        df = pd.read_csv(myfile, delimiter='\\t', header=None)",
    "execution_count": 286
  },
  {
    "id": "6c4803676288429da599fad96ce27d0b",
    "cell_type": "code",
    "source": "# Looking at the raw data\ndf.head()",
    "execution_count": 287
  },
  {
    "id": "3afffefabc3c4d1daaa1abbd452d5407",
    "cell_type": "code",
    "source": "# For each instance separate the user and their list of actions\ndf['user_id'] = df[0].str.split(':').str[0]\ndf['info'] = df[0].str.split(': ').str[1]\ndf['user_id'] = df['user_id'].str.replace('@', '')\ndf = df.drop(0, axis=1)",
    "execution_count": 288
  },
  {
    "id": "b9a6fd1561f54524bb50f7f1d9083701",
    "cell_type": "code",
    "source": "# Making list of actions with corresponding user info\ndf = df.assign(actions=df['info'].str.split('>')).explode('actions')\ndf['actions'] = df['actions'].str.strip('-')\ndf = df.drop('info', axis=1)\ndf = df.reset_index(drop=True)",
    "execution_count": 289
  },
  {
    "id": "f2ecb7e64aef47a3a37fa383e51fa8d9",
    "cell_type": "code",
    "source": "df['action_time'] = df['actions'].str.split(n=1).str[1]\ndf['action_time'] = df['action_time'].str.strip(' ')\ndf['action_name'] = df['actions'].str.split().str.get(0)\ndf = df.drop('actions', axis=1)",
    "execution_count": 290
  },
  {
    "id": "d4e77a5c83874f6d8a49a709652b1463",
    "cell_type": "code",
    "source": "df['action_time'] = pd.to_datetime(df['action_time'], format='(%d/%m/%y | %H:%M:%S)', errors='coerce')\ndf = df.sort_values(['user_id', 'action_time'])\ndf.dropna(how='any', inplace=True)",
    "execution_count": 291
  },
  {
    "id": "f5fdcb00725e43369200173f0c4f7ef9",
    "cell_type": "code",
    "source": "df['session_num'] = (df['action_name'] == 'END').groupby(df['user_id']).cumsum()",
    "execution_count": 292
  },
  {
    "id": "994dcd5710f0462a874579d9d9f016f4",
    "cell_type": "code",
    "source": "df = df[df['action_name'] != 'END']\ndf = df[df['action_name'] != 'null']\ndf.dropna(how='any', inplace=True)\ndf = df.reset_index(drop=True)",
    "execution_count": 293
  },
  {
    "id": "a6993fcfa582468198cbc719d981485a",
    "cell_type": "code",
    "source": "# The resulting dataset is as follows\ndf",
    "execution_count": 294
  },
  {
    "id": "00abbc8f75bb459e988f1dbe10a286ba",
    "cell_type": "markdown",
    "source": "# Metrics Evaluation"
  },
  {
    "id": "1275ee66167849fc86d6751c949deafa",
    "cell_type": "markdown",
    "source": "## Mean actions count per user overall"
  },
  {
    "id": "5b37a580bad5492688fbb025457d6c69",
    "cell_type": "code",
    "source": "# Each user has different number of actions.\npd.DataFrame(df.groupby('user_id')['action_time'].count()).sample(n=10)",
    "execution_count": 285
  },
  {
    "id": "88d2f2eecc0740368b883cc92db380dd",
    "cell_type": "code",
    "source": "df.groupby('user_id')['action_time'].count().mean()",
    "execution_count": 270
  },
  {
    "id": "6a4c9b1adcc04c508bf83e483e530330",
    "cell_type": "markdown",
    "source": "Average user made 13712.62 actions in the observed period."
  },
  {
    "id": "a26d2fa6ca8e4fa1a0bf0d6b128ce541",
    "cell_type": "markdown",
    "source": "## Mean actions by user in a day"
  },
  {
    "id": "a096358d23ee475983a10fa5977290bb",
    "cell_type": "code",
    "source": "df.groupby(['user_id', df['action_time'].dt.date]).size().mean()",
    "execution_count": 271
  },
  {
    "id": "0683cc6a65734b3483a225775a29d664",
    "cell_type": "markdown",
    "source": "Average user made about 28.5 actions per day in the observed period."
  },
  {
    "id": "b5a5ecbc4df3477198fad972ccb5679f",
    "cell_type": "markdown",
    "source": "## The probability of repeating the same action three times in a row during one session"
  },
  {
    "id": "616cf06955194e07baa27ac0df3a0a77",
    "cell_type": "markdown",
    "source": "## The 0.95 quantile of distribution of time delta between the actions of the same type distribution during one session"
  },
  {
    "id": "6ea88cb971f8432ab38c8f74c5b4b9d8",
    "cell_type": "markdown",
    "source": "## Is there statistical difference of activity in different days of the week? And between weekends and workdays? "
  },
  {
    "id": "e82f5761b23e468b992349aa1249b3e4",
    "cell_type": "markdown",
    "source": "For testing statistical difference of activity in different days of the week we can use ANOVA test with H0 of no significant difference."
  },
  {
    "id": "64624b91731948aa8f33e2d9d4957c22",
    "cell_type": "code",
    "source": "df['day_of_week'] = df['action_time'].dt.dayofweek\ndata = [df.loc[df['day_of_week'] == i, 'action_time'] for i in range(7)]\nf_statistic, p_value = stats.f_oneway(*data)\n\nprint(\"F-statistic:\", f_statistic)\nprint(\"p-value:\", p_value)",
    "execution_count": 301
  },
  {
    "id": "86d19c65e4364cd095697324db71e9a8",
    "cell_type": "markdown",
    "source": "In this case, the p-value is very small, which means that there is very strong evidence against the null hypothesis of no significant difference in the mean across all days of the week. There is at least one day of the week that has a significantly different mean number of actions."
  },
  {
    "id": "a8ba69360ad045e78e076b98bf1cf322",
    "cell_type": "code",
    "source": "data",
    "execution_count": 302
  },
