    "cell_type": "markdown",
    "source": "## The probability of repeating the same action three times in a row during one session"
  },
  {
    "id": "2f5e48c08aa8460885c0c994557d52a8",
    "cell_type": "markdown",
    "source": "## The 0.95 quantile of distribution of time delta between the actions of the same type distribution during one session"
  },
  {
    "id": "16fd58fe9cf74be98777c04eaac9028d",
    "cell_type": "markdown",
    "source": "## Is there statistical difference of activity in different days of the week? And between weekends and workdays? "
  },
  {
    "id": "33b002aa1ced4e0d834e5a1517c705db",
    "cell_type": "markdown",
    "source": "For testing statistical difference of activity in different days of the week we can use ANOVA test with H0 of no significant difference."
  },
  {
    "id": "67472d241f4d42c18131d6a79c0f20f8",
    "cell_type": "code",
    "source": "df['day_of_week'] = df['action_time'].dt.dayofweek\ndata = [df.loc[df['day_of_week'] == i, 'action_time'] for i in range(7)]\nf_statistic, p_value = stats.f_oneway(*data)\n\nprint(\"F-statistic:\", f_statistic)\nprint(\"p-value:\", p_value)",
    "execution_count": 301
  },
  {
    "id": "d03150feb4534af089bdf5a70fc7374d",
    "cell_type": "markdown",
    "source": "In this case, the p-value is very small, which means that there is very strong evidence against the null hypothesis of no significant difference in the mean across all days of the week. There is at least one day of the week that has a significantly different mean number of actions."
  },
